        ]
      },
      "worked": "For a whole-number square root, every index in the prime factorisation must be even. For a whole-number cube root, every index must be a multiple of 3. Thus every index must be a multiple of 6, so the number must be a sixth power.\n\nSince $64=2^6$, the next such number is $3^6=729$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{729}&=27\\\\\\sqrt[3]{729}&=9\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth roots are whole numbers, so the answer is $729$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
